# AI Kubernetes Resource Optimizer

[![Python 3.12](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.12-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/)
[![OpenAI API](https://img.shields.io/badge/OpenAI-GPT--5.6--Luna-orange.svg)](https://openai.com)
[![Kubernetes](https://img.shields.io/badge/Kubernetes-Workload_Optimization-326CE5.svg)](https://kubernetes.io/)
[![Conventional Commits](https://img.shields.io/badge/Conventional_Commits-1.0.0-yellow.svg)](https://conventionalcommits.org/)

An intelligent, two-stage AI pipeline designed to automate Kubernetes workload right-sizing. By parsing live deployment manifests alongside Prometheus alert metrics, this tool detects resource bottlenecks (CPU/memory throttling), computes precision-engineered resource blocks, and auto-generates semantic Git commit messages to streamline SRE operational workflows.

---

## 🏗️ Architecture & Pipeline Flow

The optimizer operates as a sequential multi-agent chain:

1. **Stage 1: SRE Resource Analysis (`get_optimized_resources`)**
   * **Role:** Senior Site Reliability Engineer (SRE).
   * **Input:** Original Kubernetes deployment YAML (`nginx-deployment.yaml`) and Prometheus alert metrics (`prometheus-alert.txt`).
   * **Logic:** Analyzes P99 usage profiles to mitigate throttling:
     * $\text{limits.cpu} = \text{P99} + 100\text{m}$
     * $\text{limits.memory} = \text{P99} + 50\text{Mi}$
     * $\text{requests} = \text{limits}$ (Guaranteed QoS alignment)
   * **Output:** Clean 4-line YAML `resources:` block.

2. **Stage 2: Release Manager Commit Generation (`generate_commit_message`)**
   * **Role:** Release Manager / GitOps Automation Specialist.
   * **Input:** Original YAML configuration and the newly calculated resource block.
   * **Logic:** Evaluates delta changes across compute vectors and formats a standardized git comment.
   * **Output:** A single-line Conventional Commit message (`perf: ...`).

