🚀 Getting Started
Prerequisites
Python 3.10+

Access to an OpenAI-compatible endpoint with the gpt-5.6-luna model enabled.

Installation & Environment Setup
Clone or navigate to the project directory:

Bash
cd /root/openaiproject
Create and activate a virtual environment:

Bash
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
Install dependencies:

Bash
pip install openai
Configure API Credentials:
Ensure your environment variables are set (typically loaded from /root/.bash_profile):

Bash
source /root/.bash_profile
export OPENAI_API_KEY="your-api-key"
export OPENAI_API_BASE="your-base-url"
⚙️ Usage
Execute the pipeline script directly from your terminal:

Bash
python3 k8s_optimizer.py
Example Output
Plaintext
perf: increase nginx CPU and memory requests and limits to 850m and 260Mi
🛠️ Configuration & Parameters
Model: gpt-5.6-luna (Utilized across both pipeline stages).

Stage 1 Settings: temperature=0.0, max_tokens=1000 (Deterministic calculation).

Stage 2 Settings: temperature=0.5, max_tokens=500 (Creative summarization for commit messaging).

